VERSION 2.3.2 - UI System & Code Block Enhancement

Features

- UI design system integration (major)
- Introduced centralised UI scaling system using UI(app)
- Replaced hardcoded dp and sp values with dynamic scaling
- Unified design tokens: SPACING, SPACING_SMALL, SPACING_LARGE
- Unified design tokens: ICON_SIZE, ICON_SMALL
- Unified design tokens: INPUT_HEIGHT, BUTTON_WIDTH
- Ensures consistent layout, readability and cross-platform behaviour

- Modular UI component architecture
- Refactored ArticleScreen into reusable UI builder methods
- Added StepCard component for step rendering
- Clear separation between UI composition, data rendering and styling

- Custom code font support
- Added support for bundled monospace fonts
- Implemented fallback to system fonts (DejaVuSansMono)
- Improves code readability and visual consistency

- Syntax highlighting for code blocks
- Implemented lightweight highlighting without external dependency
- Highlights comments, shell prompts, commands, options and URLs
- Uses Kivy markup system for rendering


VERSION 2.3.1 - Cross‑Platform System Integration

Features

- Cross‑platform system integration (major)
- Centralised system_open_service for opening URLs, files and asset folders
- Full support for Linux, Windows and WSL

- WSL integration support
- Automatic detection of WSL environment
- Redirects file opening to Windows Explorer and applications
- Uses Windows browser for URLs
- Path conversion handled via wslpath

- Modular architecture improvement
- Removed external system calls from main.py
- Introduced system_open_service layer
- Clear separation of UI, logic and system interactions

Improvements

- Improved installer robustness
- Refined OS detection (Debian, Arch, Fedora, WSL)
- Improved Python version validation
- Better error handling for dependencies

- WSL install optimisation
- Avoids unnecessary Linux GUI tools
- Provides WSLg setup guidance
- Skips GUI tests when not available

- Better URL handling
- Adds https:// automatically
- Decodes HTML entities
- Ensures consistent behaviour across platforms

- Improved error visibility
- Added traceback output for subprocess calls
- Eliminates silent failures

- UI responsiveness
- Removed blocking subprocess calls
- Uses async only where required

Fixes

- Fixed crash when clicking links
- Fixed missing open_url method in ArticleScreen
- Fixed incorrect indentation of method

- Fixed runtime crashes
- Fixed missing html import
- Fixed broken URL parsing logic

- Fixed WSL behaviour issues
- Corrected path conversion with wslpath
- Fixed incorrect Explorer opening
- Fixed URL opening behaviour

- Fixed UI freeze issues
- Removed blocking calls and improper threading

- Fixed inconsistent behaviour
- Unified handling of system open methods


VERSION 2.3.0 - Upgrade System & Version Tracking

Features

- Added full Upgrade App system (application updates from GitHub)
- Separated Update Data and Upgrade App
- Implemented local vs remote version tracking
- Added version.txt for installed version storage
- Installer creates version.txt on first install

Improvements

- Upgrade button reflects state (Upgrade Available / Up to Date)
- Unified button behaviour (success, failure, idle)
- Introduced version_service and update_content separation
- Improved consistency between update and upgrade workflows

Fixes

- Fixed upgrade restriction to development mode
- Fixed incorrect version display
- Fixed missing version initialisation
- Fixed AppImage detection issues


